<title>POLAND: Polish budget deficit up to PLN 5.57 bln in April.</title>
<headline>Polish budget deficit up to PLN 5.57 bln in April.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish budget deficit widened by 1.61 billion to 5.57 billion zlotys in April, which accounted for 45.6 percent of the planned 1997 deficit of 12.22 billion zlotys, the finance ministry said on Thursday.  </p>
<p> POLISH BUDGET GAP     Jan-April     Jan-March    1997 plan</p>
<p> balance in bln PLN	 5.569	    3.957	12.220</p>
<p> revenue		     32.047	   23.513     115.334</p>
<p> expenditure		 37.616	   27.470     127.554</p>
<p>NOTE: Jan-prev figures given as reported last month.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
